\subsection{HilbertCurve Permutation}
\label{sec:hilbert} 
\underline{Key idea.} Improving sparsity while maintaining accuracy is a key challenge in enhancing the performance of sparse attention. In our algorithm, increasing the self-similarity of key and query blocks can reduce the number of fix blocks.
This allows more selective blocks to participate in $\mathrm{TopCdf}$ selection, thereby improving sparsity. 
Since attention is computationally invariant to token permutations, the problem reduces to \uline{finding a permutation that enhances the similarity of adjacent tokens.}

